## Erasure (GDPR-03) — implementation hook

The right to **erasure** (Art. 17) requires that a data-subject request removes
personal data from every Store listed in `data-flow-map.md`. Wire your erasure
handler and add a test that:

1. Seeds personal data across all stores.
2. Invokes the erasure handler for a subject id.
3. Asserts no personal data for that subject remains in any store.

Reference that test here so GDPR-03 stays traceable.

## Consent / lawful basis (GDPR-04) — implementation hook

Each processing activity needs a recorded lawful basis. Where the basis is
**consent** (Art. 6(1)(a) / Art. 7), record consent capture, withdrawal, and
proof-of-consent. Reference the consent ledger and its test here.

## How the gate runs

```bash
node scripts/check-gdpr-controls.mjs   # exit 0 = all controls have evidence; exit 1 = blocking gap
```

Run automatically at L2 via `node scripts/check-all.mjs --level L2`.
